 Root Signature and Bindless
   (where RPI == Root Parameter Index)
 
 RPI        Data		Base Register

 0    		   ***		b3
 1		   ***		t0

 High level here is how you attach Resources to PSOs
 1) RPI is the sequential layout of the Root Structure Table
 2) Base Register tells you how the Shader variables will use said resources(data)

 So your task is to layout Data in Bind points and attach Base Registers to them.
 That is the purpose of Root Signatures



---  ---------- ---------- ---------- ---------- ---------- ---------- ---------- ---------- ----------
  Creating a Root Signature

Refer below how RP provides bind point and base register along with data. That's how its all tied together!!

// Important point is creating Descriptor Table(Range) requires you to provide Base Register
// When you attach this to a RPI in RS, it ties together RPI, Data and Base Register
CD3DX12_DESCRIPTOR_RANGE1 DescRange[6];
DescRange[0].Init(D3D12_DESCRIPTOR_RANGE_SRV,6,2); // t2-t7

CD3DX12_ROOT_PARAMETER1 RP[7];
RP[0].InitAsConstants(3,2); // 3 constants at b2
RP[1].InitAsDescriptorTable(2,&DescRange[0]); // 2 ranges t2-t7 and u0-u3

ID3D12RootSignature* pRootSignature;
hr = CheckHR(pDevice->CreateRootSignature(
    pSerializedRootSig->GetBufferPointer(),pSerializedRootSig->GetBufferSize(),
    __uuidof(ID3D12RootSignature),
    &pRootSignature));

